Components under their own terms
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The above covers picosdl's own code. These parts came from elsewhere and keep
the licences they arrived with:

  backend/pico/bt/          A Bluetooth HID keyboard host built on BTstack.
                            btstack_config.h is derived from the pico-examples
                            Pico W Bluetooth configuration, and kbd_host.gatt
                            follows BTstack's own example, so this directory
                            carries BSD-3-Clause material:
                              Copyright (C) 2009 BlueKitchen GmbH
                              Copyright (c) 2020 Raspberry Pi (Trading) Ltd.
                            BSD-3-Clause adds a no-endorsement clause that
                            BSD-2-Clause does not have, and it is retained here
                            rather than dropped.

  src/psdl_font9x14.inc     Generated from the X11 misc-fixed 9x15 font, whose
                            COPYING reads in full: "Public domain font. Share
                            and enjoy."

  pio-st7789/               Submodules, each with its own LICENSE file:
  pio-i2s/                  BSD-2-Clause and BSD-3-Clause respectively.

The Raspberry Pi Pico SDK, which picosdl builds against, is BSD-3-Clause and is
not distributed here.
